    "message": "Encode a loaded world once for both hashes and its restore copy\n\nVerifying a Checkpoint encoded the whole world for state_hash, encoded it\nagain inside the body for checkpoint_hash, and deep-copied it for the\nrestore. The world's canonical JSON is now encoded once: it gives\nstate_hash, is spliced into the body hash (CanonicalEncoder.remember), and\nis parsed again for the restore copy. Saved and captured documents are read\nfrom canonical JSON, so parsing it again copies them, key order included.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
